      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood began as the village of New Troy in 1833, settled by German immigrants who worked in nearby mills, tanneries, breweries, and railroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Hill_(Pittsburgh)",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1848, German Catholics founded St. Anthony's Chapel, a cornerstone of the community’s early religious life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://steelcityhistory.com/2025/06/03/the-history-of-troy-hill/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic Troy Hill Incline Building once carried commuters up the hill and now houses the Gallery Closed art project.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Hill_(Pittsburgh)",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Troy Hill’s architecture blends historic structures with contemporary construction, reflecting its evolution from an isolated hamlet to a vibrant North Side neighborhood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pittsburghplanner.com/metro-pittsburghs-best-neighborhoods-and-towns/troy-hill-neighborhood/",
